.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "wattle build"
builds images and project artifacts.
An
.Em image
is a saved module environment that
.Xr wattle-run 1
can load later.
Creating an image from a source file requires only the Wattle
runtime.
.Pp
Project artifacts are executables,
libraries and web programs declared in the project’s info
file.
Building a native executable,
a native library or a web program requires the Zig toolchain.
.Pp
.Ic b
is a synonym for
.Cm build .
.
.Ss Subcommands
The
.Cm img
subcommand takes a source file directly:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Cm img
.Xc
Loads the module at
.Ar source
and writes an image of its environment to
.Ar output .
If
.Ar output
is omitted,
it is
.Ar source
with
.Ql "\&.wattle"
replaced by
.Ql "\&.wimage" .
.Xr wattle-run 1
can be used to load the image later.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl l ,
.Fl "-lib"
.Ar module
.Xc
Imports
.Ar module
into the environment before
.Ar source
is loaded,
as
.Ic "wattle run"
does.
Several
.Fl l
options run in the order given.
.It Xo
.Fl "-depfile"
.Ar path
.Xc
Writes a Makefile rule to
.Ar path .
The image is the target,
and each file opened for reading while the modules and
.Ar source
were loaded is a prerequisite.
.Cm exe
and
.Cm web
use this rule to make an image again when a file that its source
imports or reads has changed.
.El
.El
.Pp
The other subcommands read declarations from
.Ql "info\&.edn"
in the current directory.
Generated build output is saved in
.Eo
.Pa zig-out/
.Ec
in the project root.
Copied and fetched libraries are saved in
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/
.Ec .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm exe
.Xc
Builds the executables declared with
.Ql ":type :native" .
Each program includes the Wattle runtime,
its compiled source and everything it imports.
Associated native libraries are linked into the program.
.Pp
Before building,
this subcommand copies or fetches the source and remote libraries
whose
.Ql ":for"
names the selected executables.
There is no need to run
.Cm lib
first.
If
.Ar name
is given,
only that executable is built.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl r ,
.Fl "-release"
.Ar mode
.Xc
Optimises for
.Ql "safe" ,
.Ql "fast"
or
.Ql "small" .
The default is
.Ql "safe" .
.It Xo
.Fl t ,
.Fl "-target"
.Ar triple
.Xc
Builds for
.Ar triple ,
a Zig target such as
.Ql "x86_64-linux-musl" .
The default is this machine.
.It Xo
.Fl S ,
.Fl "-no-strip"
.Xc
Keeps debug information and the static symbol table in each executable.
Without it,
both are stripped.
.It Xo
.Fl "-no-static"
.Xc
Links each executable dynamically when the target uses musl,
such as
.Ql "x86_64-linux-musl" .
Without it,
a musl executable is linked statically,
because a dynamic one needs
.Eo
.Pa /lib/ld-musl-<arch>.so.1
.Ec
at run time.
Native libraries whose
.Ql ":for"
names the executable are linked in either way,
but a static executable cannot load any other native module
at run time.
On other targets,
this option has no effect.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm lib
.Xc
Copies,
fetches or builds the declared libraries so that programs can
import them by name.
If
.Ar name
is given,
only that library is prepared.
.Pp
A source library is copied to
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/<name>.wattle
.Ec
if its
.Ql ":root"
is a file.
If the root is a directory,
its contents are copied to
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/<name>/
.Ec .
A remote library is fetched into
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/.remote/
.Ec
and then prepared as the source or native library declared in
its own info file.
A native library is built as a module in
.Eo
.Pa zig-out/lib/
.Ec .
.Pp
The
.Cm exe
subcommand also prepares its associated source and remote libraries.
.Xr wattle-run 1
does not copy,
fetch or build libraries.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl r ,
.Fl "-release"
.Ar mode
.Xc
Optimises for
.Ql "safe" ,
.Ql "fast"
or
.Ql "small" .
The default is
.Ql "safe" .
.It Xo
.Fl t ,
.Fl "-target"
.Ar triple
.Xc
Builds for
.Ar triple ,
a Zig target such as
.Ql "x86_64-linux-musl" .
The default is this machine.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm web
.Xc
Builds the executables declared with
.Ql ":type :web" .
For each executable,
the build produces a program image,
a Wattle runtime built for WebAssembly and the JavaScript needed
to run the program in a browser.
.Pp
Documentation files whose
.Ql ":for"
names the executable are copied beside the generated files.
See
.Sx "Web programs"
for the output files.
If
.Ar name
is given,
only that executable is built.
.Pp
The runtime is built for
.Ql "wasm32-wasi" ,
so this subcommand takes no
.Fl t .
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Fl r ,
.Fl "-release"
.Ar mode
.Xc
Optimises for
.Ql "safe" ,
.Ql "fast"
or
.Ql "small" .
The default is
.Ql "small" .
.El
.El
.
.Ss Zig toolchain
Building executables,
native libraries and web programs requires:
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Cm zig
to be on the user’s
.Ev PATH .
.It
The Wattle source,
which is included in Wattle releases and which is installed
to
.Eo
.Pa <prefix>/share/wattle/
.Ec .
.El
.Pp
No Zig build files are required.
.Nm "wattle build"
creates temporary
.Ql "build\&.zig"
and
.Ql "build\&.zig\&.zon"
files from the declarations in the project’s info file.
It then uses these to build with
.Cm zig .
Copying a source library needs no Zig,
and fetching a remote library needs
.Cm git
or
.Cm curl
and
.Cm tar .
.Pp
The project’s info file is
.Ql "info\&.edn"
in the current directory.
.
.Ss Project declarations
The info file declares executables,
libraries and documentation under
.Ql ":exes" ,
.Ql ":libs"
and
.Ql ":docs" .
See
.Xr wattle-projects 7
for the declaration keys,
types and examples,
and
.Xr wattle-dependencies 7
for remote libraries.
.Pp
A source executable is installed by
.Ql "wattle apps install"
and is not built by this command.
See
.Xr wattle-applications 7 .
.
.Ss Web programs
A
.Em web program
is an executable intended to run in a browser.
.Ql "wattle build web"
creates four files in
.Eo
.Pa zig-out/web/<name>/
.Ec :
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql "wattle-<hash>\&.wasm" ,
the runtime
.It
.Ql "<name>-<hash>\&.wimage" ,
the program
.It
.Ql "wasi-<hash>\&.js" ,
the WASI support shim
.It
.Ql "<name>\&.js" ,
an ES module that exports
.Ql "load"
and
.Ql "run"
.El
.Pp
Example programs are distributed with the Wattle source tree.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compile a program into an image and run the image:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle build img hello\&.wattle hello\&.wimage
$ wattle run -i hello\&.wimage Alice
.Ed
.Pp
Build the native executables that the project’s info file declares,
optimised for size:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle -p /usr/local build exe --release small
.Ed
.
